======================================================================
  4. THE PATTERN: Fix(tour) = 0 IFF EVEN CYCLE EXISTS
======================================================================

  THEOREM: Fix(sigma) = 0 for tournaments iff sigma has a 2-cycle (transposition).
  PROOF: A 2-cycle (v_0, v_1) creates the orbit {(v_0,v_1), (v_1,v_0)} on ordered pairs.
  This is self-paired: both arc directions are in the same orbit.
  For tournaments, exactly one must be present: contradiction.
  For cycles of length L >= 3: within-cycle ordered pairs are never self-paired.
  For between-cycle ordered pairs: never self-paired (different cycles).

  VERIFICATION:
    COUNTEREXAMPLE: n=4, ct=[4], has_2cycle=False, fix=0
    COUNTEREXAMPLE: n=5, ct=[4, 1], has_2cycle=False, fix=0
    COUNTEREXAMPLE: n=6, ct=[6], has_2cycle=False, fix=0
    COUNTEREXAMPLE: n=6, ct=[4, 1, 1], has_2cycle=False, fix=0
    COUNTEREXAMPLE: n=7, ct=[6, 1], has_2cycle=False, fix=0
    COUNTEREXAMPLE: n=7, ct=[4, 3], has_2cycle=False, fix=0
    COUNTEREXAMPLE: n=7, ct=[4, 1, 1, 1], has_2cycle=False, fix=0
  No counterexamples found!

